Four stores marked as integers: the scanner's position after a line comment, the id chunks, a symbol's id

A native build keeps a number field as an integer where every store to it is one it can prove an
integer (scriptc and garnet both: the `| 0` of this file's hot paths). Four stores were not: the
scanner's position from `lineCommentEnd` (a method's result), the first id of a chunk from
`Atomics.add` (twice), and a symbol's id from `takeSymbolId`. With one unproven store the field is
a double everywhere: under garnet `Scanner.pos` was converted at every token, and `Symbol.id` at
every link table lookup. Each of the four values is an int32 already; `| 0` says so.

The compiler project under garnet: 13.025 -> 12.931 G instructions on one thread (-0.72%). The
corpus: 6,537 of 6,537 cases identical.

